# Build context for the API image (Dockerfile at the repo root, `COPY . .`).
#
# Without this file the context is ~1.5 GB and nearly all of it is waste that also
# lands in the image: a macOS-built virtualenv that a python:3.11-slim Linux image
# can never use, the frontend's node_modules (the web image builds from ./web-next
# with its own .dockerignore), and the git history.
#
# Deliberately NOT ignored: ledger.db, because the api service's start command seeds
# the named volume from /app/ledger.db on first boot, and mlflow.db, which backs the
# MLFLOW_TRACKING_URI sqlite store.

# Virtualenv — 962 MB, platform-specific, reinstalled from requirements.txt anyway.
.venv/
venv/

# Frontend — built by web-next/Dockerfile, not needed by the API image.
web-next/node_modules/
web-next/.next/

# VCS and editor state.
.git/
.gitignore
.DS_Store
.claude/

# Python bytecode and test caches.
__pycache__/
**/__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/

# Evaluation outputs — regenerated, never read by the running API.
evaluation/results/
mlruns/
